  "rationale": "The spec requires 32 Msps throughput, max_abs_err <= 2^-12, and p99 batch latency <= 0.5 us. The 32 Msps constraint is the binding one: iterative (1 result per N+3 cycles) cannot meet it at any reasonable Fmax in sky130, so it will only contribute the low-area corner of the front. unrolled_k with high k (6-8) and moderate N (12-16) is the only family that can plausibly hit 32 Msps: with k=8, N=12, latency is 5 cycles/result, requiring Fmax >= 160 MHz for 32 Msps, which is aggressive but possible in sky130 for a small design. The accuracy constraint (2^-12) requires N >= ~13-14 iterations or data_width >= 14 with rounding. I allocate 55% of budget to unrolled_k (the feasible family) and 45% to iterative (the area-floor family). angle_guard is fixed at 0 to minimize area since the accuracy constraint is met by n_iter/data_width alone. frac_guard is searched 0-4 to capture the area/accuracy trade-off. Both rounding modes are included since rounding can save 1 bit of n_iter. data_width 14-28 and n_iter 12-30 cover the accuracy constraint with margin."
